=== HINT 1: Open MD4 provider ===
BCRYPT_ALG_HANDLE hAlg = NULL;
BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider(&hAlg, BCRYPT_MD4_ALGORITHM, NULL, 0);

=== HINT 2: Hash the UTF-16 password ===
BCRYPT_HASH_HANDLE hHash = NULL;
BCryptCreateHash(hAlg, &hHash, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0);
BCryptHashData(hHash, (PUCHAR)pw, pw_bytes, 0);
BCryptFinishHash(hHash, hash, sizeof(hash), 0);

=== HINT 3: Print hex ===
for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++) printf("%02x", hash[i]);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
NTLM hash = MD4(UTF-16-LE(password)) - no salt, no iteration, trivially rainbow-tabled.
LM hash = DES(split password into 7-char chunks, uppercase) - even weaker, disabled Win Vista+.
Pass-the-hash with actual auth:
  - SMB: use impacket's smbclient.py/psexec.py -hashes LM:NT target
  - WinRM: evil-winrm with -H (NT hash)
  - LDAP: ldap3/impacket with NTLM authentication
Windows API PtH: mimikatz sekurlsa::pth patches LSASS credentials directly.
Overpass-the-Hash: use NT hash to request a Kerberos TGT (kinit with hash).
Pass-the-Ticket: export Kerberos TGT/TGS and import on another machine.
